# Tool state this profile's tools write in the checkout, never the run's work (agent_job.sh excludes): kept out of
# the agent's git status and out of the bundle step's check for uncommitted changes. One plain pattern a line.
#
# ASP.NET Core keeps its data protection keys and its development certificate's trust under HOME's .aspnet/. In the
# pilot project's first implement run, a .aspnet/ appeared beside the server project once its end-to-end specs had
# started the server, and stopped the publish. A relative HOME does that, as reproduced with HOME=.; install.sh's
# LOCALAPPDATA now sends the keys into .factory/, and this catches anything else that resolves the home the same
# way. verify probe prints what HOME a sandboxed command has.
.aspnet/
